   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Shader Dithering\n\nAn animated gradient field rendered as a two-color ordered dither, like 1-bit print or an old screen: a lo-fi WebGL backdrop.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 5 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- You want a retro or print-like 1-bit ordered-dither texture over a moving gradient.\n- A tech or lo-fi scene benefits from visible Bayer dot structure; pick the matrix with `type`.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You want a centered dithered sphere: set `shape` to sphere (the default is the full-bleed wave).\n- You want smooth, untextured color: use shader-mesh-gradient.\n- The dot pattern would hurt the legibility of small text: raise `size` or use a solid backdrop.\n\nVariables:\n- color_back (color): Background, default \"#12121a\"\n- color_front (color): Front, default \"#6a6a85\"\n- shape (enum): Shape, default \"wave\"\n- type (enum): Dither, default \"4x4\"\n- size (number, 1-8): Dot size, default 2\n- speed (number, 0-4): Speed, default 1\n- rotation (number, 0-360): Rotation, default 0\n- scale (number, 0.1-4): Scale, default 0.6\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.5\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Shader Dithering\n\n  A moving gradient field drawn in two colors with an ordered (Bayer) dither: a retro, 1-bit print texture.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/shader-dithering/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n\n  The vertex and fragment shaders below are from Paper Shaders\n  (@paper-design/shaders 0.0.82, dist/vertex-shader.js and dist/shaders/dithering.js),\n  https://github.com/paper-design/shaders\n\n  Copyright 2026 Paper. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");\n  you may not use this file except in compliance with the License. You may obtain a copy\n  of the License at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Unless required by\n  applicable law or agreed to in writing, software distributed under the License is\n  distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either\n  express or implied. See the License for the specific language governing permissions\n  and limitations under the License.\n\n  NOTICE: Paper Shaders. Copyright 2026 Paper. Powered by Paper Shaders:\n  https://shaders.paper.design\n\n  Changes by usemosio/blocks: the shared GLSL helpers are inlined, the vertex shader keeps only\n  the outputs the fragment shader reads, and the shader mount is rewritten: the canvas is drawn at\n  a reduced resolution (the `resolution` variable) and its time comes from the timeline. The\n  canvas is scaled up without smoothing so the dots stay sharp.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"shader-dithering\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    { \"id\": \"color_back\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Color of the empty dots.\", \"default\": \"#12121a\" },\n    { \"id\": \"color_front\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Front\", \"description\": \"Color of the lit dots.\", \"default\": \"#6a6a85\" },\n    { \"id\": \"shape\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Shape\", \"description\": \"The gradient field under the dither.\", \"default\": \"wave\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"simplex\", \"label\": \"Simplex noise\"}, {\"value\": \"warp\", \"label\": \"Warp\"}, {\"value\": \"dots\", \"label\": \"Dots\"}, {\"value\": \"wave\", \"label\": \"Wave\"}, {\"value\": \"ripple\", \"label\": \"Ripple\"}, {\"value\": \"swirl\", \"label\": \"Swirl\"}, {\"value\": \"sphere\", \"label\": \"Sphere\"}] },\n    { \"id\": \"type\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Dither\", \"description\": \"Dither matrix: random noise or an ordered Bayer grid.\", \"default\": \"4x4\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"random\", \"label\": \"Random\"}, {\"value\": \"2x2\", \"label\": \"Bayer 2×2\"}, {\"value\": \"4x4\", \"label\": \"Bayer 4×4\"}, {\"value\": \"8x8\", \"label\": \"Bayer 8×8\"}] },\n    { \"id\": \"size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Dot size\", \"description\": \"Size of one dither dot in pixels.\", \"default\": 2, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 8, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\" },\n    { \"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"How fast the field moves. 0 holds still.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05 },\n    { \"id\": \"rotation\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Rotation\", \"description\": \"Turns the field.\", \"default\": 0, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 360, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"deg\" },\n    { \"id\": \"scale\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Scale\", \"description\": \"Zooms the field in or out.\", \"default\": 0.6, \"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.01 },\n    { \"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up without smoothing. It is rounded so every dither dot covers whole pixels, so 0.5 with size 2 looks the same as 1.\", \"default\": 0.5, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05 }\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Shader Dithering</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: var(--sdi-fallback, #12121a);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .sdi-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .sdi-canvas {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n          image-rendering: pixelated;\n        }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"shader-dithering\" data-duration=\"5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"sdi-clip\" class=\"sdi-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"sdi-canvas\" class=\"sdi-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"sdi-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function parseColor(s) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6}|[0-9a-f]{8})$/i.exec(String(s).trim());\n              if (!m) return null;\n              var h = m[1];\n              if (h.length === 3) h = h[0] + h[0] + h[1] + h[1] + h[2] + h[2];\n              var a = h.length === 8 ? parseInt(h.slice(6, 8), 16) / 255 : 1;\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255, a];\n            }\n            function color(value, fallback) {\n              return parseColor(value) || parseColor(fallback);\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function css(c) {\n              return \"rgba(\" + Math.round(c[0] * 255) + \",\" + Math.round(c[1] * 255) + \",\" + Math.round(c[2] * 255) + \",\" + c[3] + \")\";\n            }\n            var colorBack = color(vars.color_back, \"#12121a\");\n            var colorFront = color(vars.color_front, \"#6a6a85\");\n            var shape = pick(vars.shape, [\"simplex\", \"warp\", \"dots\", \"wave\", \"ripple\", \"swirl\", \"sphere\"], \"wave\");\n            var type = pick(vars.type, [\"random\", \"2x2\", \"4x4\", \"8x8\"], \"4x4\");\n            var size = num(vars.size, 2, 1, 8);\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0, 4);\n            var rotation = num(vars.rotation, 0, 0, 360);\n            var scale = num(vars.scale, 0.6, 0.1, 4);\n            var resolution = num(vars.resolution, 0.5, 0.25, 1);\n            // Each dither dot must cover whole canvas pixels, or the pattern breaks up when scaled.\n            resolution = Math.min(1, Math.max(1, Math.round(size * resolution)) / size);\n            var SHAPES = { simplex: 1, warp: 2, dots: 3, wave: 4, ripple: 5, swirl: 6, sphere: 7 };\n            var TYPES = { random: 1, \"2x2\": 2, \"4x4\": 3, \"8x8\": 4 };\n\n            // Without WebGL the block still shows the palette as a plain gradient.\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--sdi-fallback\", \"linear-gradient(160deg, \" + [colorBack, colorFront].map(css).join(\", \") + \")\");\n\n            // Paper Shaders vertex shader, only the outputs the fragment shader reads.\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"precision mediump float;\",\n              \"layout(location = 0) in vec4 a_position;\",\n              \"uniform vec2 u_resolution;\",\n              \"uniform float u_pixelRatio;\",\n              \"uniform float u_originX;\",\n              \"uniform float u_originY;\",\n              \"uniform float u_worldWidth;\",\n              \"uniform float u_worldHeight;\",\n              \"uniform float u_fit;\",\n              \"uniform float u_scale;\",\n              \"uniform float u_rotation;\",\n              \"uniform float u_offsetX;\",\n              \"uniform float u_offsetY;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"vec3 getBoxSize(float boxRatio, vec2 givenBoxSize) {\",\n              \"  vec2 box = vec2(0.);\",\n              \"  box.x = boxRatio * min(givenBoxSize.x / boxRatio, givenBoxSize.y);\",\n              \"  float noFitBoxWidth = box.x;\",\n              \"  if (u_fit == 1.) { box.x = boxRatio * min(u_resolution.x / boxRatio, u_resolution.y); }\",\n              \"  else if (u_fit == 2.) { box.x = boxRatio * max(u_resolution.x / boxRatio, u_resolution.y); }\",\n              \"  box.y = box.x / boxRatio;\",\n              \"  return vec3(box, noFitBoxWidth);\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  gl_Position = a_position;\",\n              \"  vec2 uv = gl_Position.xy * .5;\",\n              \"  vec2 boxOrigin = vec2(.5 - u_originX, u_originY - .5);\",\n              \"  vec2 givenBoxSize = vec2(u_worldWidth, u_worldHeight);\",\n              \"  givenBoxSize = max(givenBoxSize, vec2(1.)) * u_pixelRatio;\",\n              \"  float r = u_rotation * 3.14159265358979323846 / 180.;\",\n              \"  mat2 graphicRotation = mat2(cos(r), sin(r), -sin(r), cos(r));\",\n              \"  vec2 graphicOffset = vec2(-u_offsetX, u_offsetY);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n\n            // Paper Shaders dithering fragment shader.\n            var FRAGMENT = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"precision mediump float;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"uniform float u_time;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"uniform vec2 u_resolution;\",\n              \"uniform float u_pixelRatio;\",\n              \"uniform float u_originX;\",\n              \"uniform float u_originY;\",\n              \"uniform float u_worldWidth;\",\n              \"uniform float u_worldHeight;\",\n              \"uniform float u_fit;\",\n              \"uniform float u_scale;\",\n              \"uniform float u_rotation;\",\n              \"uniform float u_offsetX;\",\n              \"uniform float u_offsetY;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"uniform float u_pxSize;\",\n              \"uniform vec4 u_colorBack;\",\n              \"uniform vec4 u_colorFront;\",\n              \"uniform float u_shape;\",\n              \"uniform float u_type;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"out vec4 fragColor;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"vec3 permute(vec3 x) { return mod(((x * 34.0) + 1.0) * x, 289.0); }\",\n              \"float snoise(vec2 v) {\",\n              \"  const vec4 C = vec4(0.211324865405187, 0.366025403784439,\",\n              \"    -0.577350269189626, 0.024390243902439);\",\n              \"  vec2 i = floor(v + dot(v, C.yy));\",\n              \"  vec2 x0 = v - i + dot(i, C.xx);\",\n              \"  vec2 i1;\",\n              \"  i1 = (x0.x > x0.y) ? vec2(1.0, 0.0) : vec2(0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"  vec4 x12 = x0.xyxy + C.xxzz;\",\n              \"  x12.xy -= i1;\",\n              \"  i = mod(i, 289.0);\",\n              \"  vec3 p = permute(permute(i.y + vec3(0.0, i1.y, 1.0))\",\n              \"    + i.x + vec3(0.0, i1.x, 1.0));\",\n              \"  vec3 m = max(0.5 - vec3(dot(x0, x0), dot(x12.xy, x12.xy),\",\n              \"      dot(x12.zw, x12.zw)), 0.0);\",\n              \"  m = m * m;\",\n              \"  m = m * m;\",\n              \"  vec3 x = 2.0 * fract(p * C.www) - 1.0;\",\n              \"  vec3 h = abs(x) - 0.5;\",\n              \"  vec3 ox = floor(x + 0.5);\",\n              \"  vec3 a0 = x - ox;\",\n              \"  m *= 1.79284291400159 - 0.85373472095314 * (a0 * a0 + h * h);\",\n              \"  vec3 g;\",\n              \"  g.x = a0.x * x0.x + h.x * x0.y;\",\n              \"  g.yz = a0.yz * x12.xz + h.yz * x12.yw;\",\n              \"  return 130.0 * dot(m, g);\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"#define TWO_PI 6.28318530718\",\n              \"#define PI 3.14159265358979323846\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float hash11(float p) {\",\n              \"    p = fract(p * 0.3183099) + 0.1;\",\n              \"    p *= p + 19.19;\",\n              \"    return fract(p * p);\",\n              \"  }\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float hash21(vec2 p) {\",\n              \"    p = fract(p * vec2(0.3183099, 0.3678794)) + 0.1;\",\n              \"    p += dot(p, p + 19.19);\",\n              \"    return fract(p.x * p.y);\",\n              \"  }\",\n              \"\",\n              \"float getSimplexNoise(vec2 uv, float t) {\",\n              \"  float noise = .5 * snoise(uv - vec2(0., .3 * t));\",\n              \"  noise += .5 * snoise(2. * uv + vec2(0., .32 * t));\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  return noise;\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"const int bayer2x2[4] = int[4](0, 2, 3, 1);\",\n              \"const int bayer4x4[16] = int[16](\",\n              \"0, 8, 2, 10,\",\n              \"12, 4, 14, 6,\",\n              \"3, 11, 1, 9,\",\n              \"15, 7, 13, 5\",\n              \");\",\n              \"\",\n              \"const int bayer8x8[64] = int[64](\",\n              \"0, 32, 8, 40, 2, 34, 10, 42,\",\n              \"48, 16, 56, 24, 50, 18, 58, 26,\",\n              \"12, 44, 4, 36, 14, 46, 6, 38,\",\n              \"60, 28, 52, 20, 62, 30, 54, 22,\",\n              \"3, 35, 11, 43, 1, 33, 9, 41,\",\n              \"51, 19, 59, 27, 49, 17, 57, 25,\",\n              \"15, 47, 7, 39, 13, 45, 5, 37,\",\n              \"63, 31, 55, 23, 61, 29, 53, 21\",\n              \");\",\n              \"\",\n              \"float getBayerValue(vec2 uv, int size) {\",\n              \"  ivec2 pos = ivec2(fract(uv / float(size)) * float(size));\",\n              \"  int index = pos.y * size + pos.x;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  if (size == 2) {\",\n              \"    return float(bayer2x2[index]) / 4.0;\",\n              \"  } else if (size == 4) {\",\n              \"    return float(bayer4x4[index]) / 16.0;\",\n              \"  } else if (size == 8) {\",\n              \"    return float(bayer8x8[index]) / 64.0;\",\n              \"  }\",\n              \"  return 0.0;\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  float t = .5 * u_time;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float pxSize = u_pxSize * u_pixelRatio;\",\n              \"  vec2 pxSizeUV = gl_FragCoord.xy - .5 * u_resolution;\",\n              \"  pxSizeUV /= pxSize;\",\n              \"  vec2 canvasPixelizedUV = (floor(pxSizeUV) + .5) * pxSize;\",\n              \"  vec2 normalizedUV = canvasPixelizedUV / u_resolution;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  vec2 ditheringNoiseUV = canvasPixelizedUV;\",\n              \"  vec2 shapeUV = normalizedUV;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  vec2 boxOrigin = vec2(.5 - u_originX, u_originY - .5);\",\n              \"  vec2 givenBoxSize = vec2(u_worldWidth, u_worldHeight);\",\n              \"  givenBoxSize = max(givenBoxSize, vec2(1.)) * u_pixelRatio;\",\n              \"  float r = u_rotation * PI / 180.;\",\n              \"  mat2 graphicRotation = mat2(cos(r), sin(r), -sin(r), cos(r));\",\n              \"  vec2 graphicOffset = vec2(-u_offsetX, u_offsetY);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float patternBoxRatio = givenBoxSize.x / givenBoxSize.y;\",\n              \"  vec2 boxSize = vec2(\",\n              \"  (u_worldWidth == 0.) ? u_resolution.x : givenBoxSize.x,\",\n              \"  (u_worldHeight == 0.) ? u_resolution.y : givenBoxSize.y\",\n              \"  );\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  if (u_shape > 3.5) {\",\n              \"    vec2 objectBoxSize = vec2(0.);\",\n              \"    // fit = none\",\n              \"    objectBoxSize.x = min(boxSize.x, boxSize.y);\",\n              \"    if (u_fit == 1.) { // fit = contain\",\n              \"      objectBoxSize.x = min(u_resolution.x, u_resolution.y);\",\n              \"    } else if (u_fit == 2.) { // fit = cover\",\n              \"      objectBoxSize.x = max(u_resolution.x, u_resolution.y);\",\n              \"    }\",\n              \"    objectBoxSize.y = objectBoxSize.x;\",\n              \"    vec2 objectWorldScale = u_resolution.xy / objectBoxSize;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"    shapeUV *= objectWorldScale;\",\n              \"    shapeUV += boxOrigin * (objectWorldScale - 1.);\",\n              \"    shapeUV += vec2(-u_offsetX, u_offsetY);\",\n              \"    shapeUV /= u_scale;\",\n              \"    shapeUV = graphicRotation * shapeUV;\",\n              \"  } else {\",\n              \"    vec2 patternBoxSize = vec2(0.);\",\n              \"    // fit = none\",\n              \"    patternBoxSize.x = patternBoxRatio * min(boxSize.x / patternBoxRatio, boxSize.y);\",\n              \"    float patternWorldNoFitBoxWidth = patternBoxSize.x;\",\n              \"    if (u_fit == 1.) { // fit = contain\",\n              \"      patternBoxSize.x = patternBoxRatio * min(u_resolution.x / patternBoxRatio, u_resolution.y);\",\n              \"    } else if (u_fit == 2.) { // fit = cover\",\n              \"      patternBoxSize.x = patternBoxRatio * max(u_resolution.x / patternBoxRatio, u_resolution.y);\",\n              \"    }\",\n              \"    patternBoxSize.y = patternBoxSize.x / patternBoxRatio;\",\n              \"    vec2 patternWorldScale = u_resolution.xy / patternBoxSize;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"    shapeUV += vec2(-u_offsetX, u_offsetY) / patternWorldScale;\",\n              \"    shapeUV += boxOrigin;\",\n              \"    shapeUV -= boxOrigin / patternWorldScale;\",\n              \"    shapeUV *= u_resolution.xy;\",\n              \"    shapeUV /= u_pixelRatio;\",\n              \"    if (u_fit > 0.) {\",\n              \"      shapeUV *= (patternWorldNoFitBoxWidth / patternBoxSize.x);\",\n              \"    }\",\n              \"    shapeUV /= u_scale;\",\n              \"    shapeUV = graphicRotation * shapeUV;\",\n              \"    shapeUV += boxOrigin / patternWorldScale;\",\n              \"    shapeUV -= boxOrigin;\",\n              \"    shapeUV += .5;\",\n              \"  }\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float shape = 0.;\",\n              \"  if (u_shape < 1.5) {\",\n              \"    // Simplex noise\",\n              \"    shapeUV *= .001;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"    shape = 0.5 + 0.5 * getSimplexNoise(shapeUV, t);\",\n              \"    shape = smoothstep(0.3, 0.9, shape);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  } else if (u_shape < 2.5) {\",\n              \"    // Warp\",\n              \"    shapeUV *= .003;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"    for (float i = 1.0; i < 6.0; i++) {\",\n              \"      shapeUV.x += 0.6 / i * cos(i * 2.5 * shapeUV.y + t);\",\n              \"      shapeUV.y += 0.6 / i * cos(i * 1.5 * shapeUV.x + t);\",\n              \"    }\",\n              \"\",\n              \"    shape = .15 / max(0.001, abs(sin(t - shapeUV.y - shapeUV.x)));\",\n              \"    shape = smoothstep(0.02, 1., shape);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  } else if (u_shape < 3.5) {\",\n              \"    // Dots\",\n              \"    shapeUV *= .05;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"    float stripeIdx = floor(2. * shapeUV.x / TWO_PI);\",\n              \"    float rand = hash11(stripeIdx * 10.);\",\n              \"    rand = sign(rand - .5) * pow(.1 + abs(rand), .4);\",\n              \"    shape = sin(shapeUV.x) * cos(shapeUV.y - 5. * rand * t);\",\n              \"    shape = pow(abs(shape), 6.);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  } else if (u_shape < 4.5) {\",\n              \"    // Sine wave\",\n              \"    shapeUV *= 4.;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"    float wave = cos(.5 * shapeUV.x - 2. * t) * sin(1.5 * shapeUV.x + t) * (.75 + .25 * cos(3. * t));\",\n              \"    shape = 1. - smoothstep(-1., 1., shapeUV.y + wave);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  } else if (u_shape < 5.5) {\",\n              \"    // Ripple\",\n           